{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/","folio-assistant-sci":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant-sci/v0/ns/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-r-matrix-braiding-structure","@type":["folio-assistant-sci:Proposition","doco:Section"],"label":"prop:r-matrix-braiding-structure","kind":"proposition","title":"Yang--Baxter equation and braid operator from the $R$-matrix","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-quantum-su2","papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-braid-twist-flip"],"examples":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/rem-r-matrix-braiding","papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/rem-skein-crossing-asymmetry"],"tags":["r-matrix","yang-baxter","quantum-group","braiding"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.Braiding.r_matrix_braiding_structure","text":"r-matrix-braiding-structure.md","leanSource":"r-matrix-braiding-structure.lean","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"prop:r-matrix-braiding-structure\"></a><p>The universal <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">R</code>-matrix <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathcal{R} \\in \\mathcal{U}_q(\\mathfrak{su}(2)) \\hat{\\otimes} \\mathcal{U}_q(\\mathfrak{su}(2))</code> satisfies the Yang--Baxter equation:</p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-math math-display\">  \\mathcal{R}_{12}\\mathcal{R}_{13}\\mathcal{R}_{23}\n  = \n  \\mathcal{R}_{23}\\mathcal{R}_{13}\\mathcal{R}_{12}.</code></pre>\n<p>The braid operator <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\check{R} = P \\circ \\mathcal{R}</code> (with <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">P</code> the tensor swap) furnishes a representation of the braid group on any tensor product of finite-dimensional <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathcal{U}_q(\\mathfrak{su}(2))</code>-modules.</p>\n<p>The underlying <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">R</code>-matrix theory is standard; the eigenvalues <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q</code> and <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">-q^{-1}</code> (the Hecke channels) provide the tie-in to the physical observable structure.</p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/r-matrix-braiding-structure.md","heading":"Proposition","number":"7.9.9","page":"b/prop-r-matrix-braiding-structure","qa":{"counts":{"pass":99,"fail":1,"warn":1,"na":17,"unknown":0,"stale":94},"milnor":{"total":3,"notPassing":0}},"lean":{"expected":true,"ref":"qou:BraidKnotOctonion.r_matrix_braiding_structure","via":"sibling","path":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/r-matrix-braiding-structure.lean","compiles":"unchecked","sorry":false,"sorryBasis":"text"}}
